{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift imports any function declared in a C header as a Swift global function.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, consider the following C function declarations:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["int product(int multiplier, int multiplicand);","int quotient(int dividend, int divisor, int *remainder);","","struct Point2D createPoint2D(float x, float y);","float distance(struct Point2D from, struct Point2D to);"],"syntax":"occ"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s how Swift imports them:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func product(_ multiplier: Int32, _ multiplicand: Int32) -> Int32","func quotient(_ dividend: Int32, _ divisor: Int32, _ remainder: UnsafeMutablePointer<Int32>) -> Int32","","func createPoint2D(_ x: Float, _ y: Float) -> Point2D","func distance(_ from: Point2D, _ to: Point2D) -> Float"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Use-a-CVaListPointer-to-Call-Variadic-Functions","text":"Use a CVaListPointer to Call Variadic Functions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Swift, you can call C variadic functions, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"vasprintf(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/getVaList(_:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withVaList(_:_:)"},{"text":" functions. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"withVaList(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function takes an array of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVarArg"},{"text":" values and provides a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVaListPointer"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value within the body of a closure parameter, whereas the ","type":"text"},{"code":"getVaList(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns this value directly. With either function, you pass the resulting ","type":"text"},{"code":"CVaListPointer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value as the ","type":"text"},{"code":"va_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" argument of the C variadic function.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, here’s how to call the ","type":"text"},{"code":"vasprintf(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function in Swift:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func swiftprintf(format: String, arguments: CVarArg...) -> String? {","    return withVaList(arguments) { va_list in","        var buffer: UnsafeMutablePointer<Int8>? = nil","        return format.withCString { cString in","            guard vasprintf(&buffer, cString, va_list) != 0 else {","                return nil","            }","","            return String(validatingUTF8: buffer!)","        }","    }","}","print(swiftprintf(format: \"√2 ≅ %g\", arguments: sqrt(2.0))!)","\/\/ Prints \"√2 ≅ 1.41421\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift only imports C variadic functions that use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"va_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":